course: dictionary
lesson: 16173
title: The feeling of wrongness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wrongness is a noun. It names the quality of being wrong. It has two main meanings. The first is about right and wrong for people: «The class talked about the wrongness of cheating.» The second is about things being incorrect or not as they should be.
explain: You cannot count wrongness, so you do not say "three wrongnesses." You can say «a sense of wrongness» or «a feeling of wrongness» when something seems not quite right, even if you cannot say exactly why.
explain: Stories often use wrongness to warn the reader. «The house was silent, and Mia felt a strange wrongness in the air.» The clues are silent and strange. The writer is telling you that something bad may be coming. When you meet wrongness, ask: is this about right and wrong, or about something not being as it should be?
fact: Wrongness means the quality of being wrong.
fact: «Wrongness» can mean morally wrong or unfair, as in «the wrongness of stealing».
fact: «Wrongness» can also mean incorrect or not as it should be, as in «a feeling of wrongness».
fact: Wrongness is uncountable, so you say «a sense of wrongness», not «wrongnesses».
fact: Wrong is the adjective, and wrongness is the noun made from it.
exercise: «The teacher asked the class to think about the wrongness of cheating in the test.» What does wrongness mean here? | The quality of being very loud | The quality of being shiny | The quality of being very fast | *The quality of being morally wrong or unfair
exercise: «The sums were full of mistakes, and Sam noticed a wrongness in every line.» What does wrongness mean here? | *The quality of being incorrect | The quality of being very neat | The quality of being quick | The quality of being bright
exercise: Which phrase uses wrongness correctly? | Two wrongnesses | Many wrongnesses | Wrongnesses are fun | *A sense of wrongness
test: «The wrongness of lying to a friend can really hurt them.» What does wrongness mean here? | Being very tall | Being quick at maths | Being very cold | *Being morally wrong or unfair
test: Which word is the noun for the quality of being wrong? | Wrongful | Wrongly | *Wrongness | Wrong
exam: Read: «Tom felt a wrongness in the silent house, as if something was about to happen.» What does this tell the reader? | The house is brand new | Tom is very hungry | The lights are very bright | *Something bad is probably about to happen
